samples from multiple equilibrium states.</article-title><source>J Chem Phys</source><volume>129</volume><fpage>124105</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">19045004</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0005840-Kumar1"><label>22</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kumar</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Bouzida</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Swendsen</surname><given-names>RH</given-names></name><name><surname>Kollman</surname><given-names>PA</given-names></name><name><surname>Rosenberg</surname><given-names>JM</given-names></name></person-group><year>1992</year><article-title>The Weighted Histogram Analysis Method for Free-Energy Calculations on Biomolecules.1. The Method.</article-title><source>J Comp Chem</source><volume>13</volume><fpage>1011</fpage><lpage>1021</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0005840-Derrick1"><label>23</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Derrick</surname><given-names>JP</given-names></name><name><surname>Wigley</surname><given-names>DB</given-names></name></person-group><year>1994</year><article-title>The third IgG-binding domain from streptococcal protein G. An analysis by X-ray crystallography of the structure alone and in a complex with Fab.</article-title><source>J Mol Biol</source><volume>243</volume><fpage>906</fpage><lpage>918</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7966308</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0005840-Clarke1"><label>24</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Clarke</surname><given-names>ND</given-names></name><name><surname>Kissinger</surname><given-names>CR</given-names></name><name><surname>Desjarlais</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Gilliland</surname><given-names>GL</given-names></name><name><surname>Pabo</surname><given-names>CO</given-names></name></person-group><year>1994</year><article-title>Structural studies of the engrailed homeodomain.</article-title><source>Protein Sci</source><volume>3</volume><fpage>1779</fpage><lpage>1787</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7849596</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0005840-Kortemme1"><label>25</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kortemme</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Morozov</surname><given-names>AV</given-names></name><name><surname>Baker</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name></person-group><year>2003</year><article-title>An orientation-dependent hydrogen bonding potential improves prediction of specificity and structure for proteins and protein-protein complexes.</article-title><source>J Mol Biol</source><volume>326</volume><fpage>1239</fpage><lpage>1259</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12589766</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0005840-Morozov1"><label>26</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Morozov</surname><given-names>AV</given-names></name><name><surname>Kortemme</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Tsemekhman</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Baker</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name></person-group><year>2004</year><article-title>Close agreement between the orientation dependence of hydrogen bonds observed in protein structures and quantum mechanical calculations.</article-title><source>Proc Natl Acad Sci USA</source><volume>101</volume><fpage>6946</fpage><lpage>6951</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15118103</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0005840-Chiu1"><label>27</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Chiu</surname><given-names>TK</given-names></name><name><surname>Kubelka</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Herbst-Irmer</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Eaton</surname><given-names>WA</given-names></name><name><surname>Hofrichter</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2005</year><article-title>High-resolution x-ray crystal structures of the villin headpiece subdomain, an ultrafast folding protein.</article-title><source>Proc Natl Acad Sci USA</source><volume>102</volume><fpage>7517</fpage><lpage>7522</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15894611</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0005840-Tsai1"><label>28</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Tsai</surname><given-names>CJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Maizel</surname><given-names>JV</given-names></name><name><surname>Nussinov</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><year>2000</year><article-title>Anatomy of protein structures: Visualizing how a one-dimensional protein chain folds into a three-dimensional shape.</article-title><source>Proc Natl Acad Sci USA</source><volume>97</volume><fpage>12038</fpage><lpage>12043</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11050234</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0005840-Haspel1"><label>29</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Haspel</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Tsai</surname><given-names>CJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Wolfson</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Nussinov</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><year>2003</year><article-title>Reducing the computational complexity of protein folding via fragment folding and assembly.</article-title><source>Protein Sci</source><volume>12</volume><fpage>1177</fpage><lpage>1187</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12761388</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0005840-Kifer1"><label>30</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kifer</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name><name><surname>Nussinov</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Wolfson</surname><given-names>HJ</given-names></name></person-group><year>2008</year><article-title>Constructing templates for protein structure prediction by simulation of protein folding pathways.</article-title><source>Proteins</source><volume>73</volume><fpage>380</fpage><lpage>394</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">18433063</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0005840-Humphrey1"><label>31</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Humphrey</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name><name><surname>Dalke</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Schulten</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name></person-group><year>1996</year><article-title>VMD: visual molecular dynamics.</article-title><source>J Mol Graph</source><volume>14</volume><fpage>33</fpage><lpage>8</lpage><page-range>27&#x02013;8</page-range><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8744570</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list><fn-group><fn fn-type="conflict"><p><bold>Competing Interests: </bold>The authors have declared that no competing interests exist.</p></fn><fn fn-type="financial-disclosure"><p><bold>Funding: </bold>Computer resources were provided by NSF award CNS-0619926. This work was also funded by NSF CHE-0535616 and NIH R01-GM062868. G. Bowman was funded by the NSF Graduate Research Fellowship Program. The funders had no role in study design, data collection and analysis, decision to publish, or preparation of the manuscript.</p></fn></fn-group></back></article>